        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "lM9hV",
          "x": 1429,
          "y": 39,
          "name": "Confirmation — restore defaults",
          "context": "Firmware behavior (source/Core/Src/settingsGUI.cpp:481-508, 1077-1087): userConfirmation accepts F_SHORT or OK_SHORT to confirm; it cancels on B_SHORT, F_LONG, B_LONG, OK_LONG, or BOTH. There is no timeout. Confirming calls resetSettings(), displays a success warning until dismissal, then reboots. The on-screen mapping emphasizes OK: Reset and Hold OK: Cancel; F_SHORT is an alternate confirm input. The firmware English prompt is “Are you sure you want to restore default settings?” No hold-to-reset safeguard or selected Yes/No state exists. Typography: Space Grotesk only, using existing size tokens (15px settings labels, 19px settings values, and 30px temperature digits where needed), weight 600. Reuse raster glyph sets; do not introduce utility-only 12px or 24px font sizes. Verified at native 160x80 canvas size; hardware legibility remains to be checked on-device.",
